t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t<\/section>\n\t\t\t\t<section class=\"elementor-section elementor-top-section elementor-element elementor-element-eb45111 elementor-section-boxed elementor-section-height-default elementor-section-height-default\" data-id=\"eb45111\" data-element_type=\"section\" data-settings=\"{&quot;jet_parallax_layout_list&quot;:[]}\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-container elementor-column-gap-default\">\n\t\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-column elementor-col-100 elementor-top-column elementor-element elementor-element-f2d0b89\" data-id=\"f2d0b89\" data-element_type=\"column\">\n\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-widget-wrap elementor-element-populated\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-3d8091f elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"3d8091f\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\">\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-widget-container\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<p>Dr. David Cox, VP of Data Science at RethinkBH, has worked within the behavioral health industry for over 17 years. Dr. Cox received his Ph.D. in Behavior Analysis from the University of Florida, post-doctoral training in behavioral pharmacology &amp; behavioral economics from John Hopkins University School of Medicine, and post-doctoral training in Data Science from Insight! Data Science program.<\/p><p>Since 2014 his work has focused on how to effectively leverage technology, quantitative modeling, and artificial intelligence to ethically optimize behavioral health outcomes and clinical decision-making. He joins us today to talk about artificial intelligence and its implications within the field of ABA.<\/p>\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t<\/section>\n\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t","protected":false},"author":19,"featured_media":23052,"template":"","meta":{"_seopress_robots_primary_cat":"","_seopress_titles_title":"Podcast: AI in Applied Behavior Analysis (